From 7615b69a744af7e79068a7bcc9968783aac62a3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 22:13:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 89/89] video: rockchip: harden IEP2 lifetimes and DMA bounds

Synchronize timeout and provider callback teardown before task or device storage can be freed. Protect IEP2 current-task access, make clock/reset failures fatal, and close raw-address and undersized-buffer submission paths.

Keep the I1O1T auxiliary mapping inside task and IOVA allocator lifetime, using an exclusive reservation primitive so cleanup never removes another DMA allocation's node. Suppress unsupported MPP hot-unbind entry points until the common service has a complete drain/unpublish contract.
